Changes made by OSB (GPL-2.0-or-later, section 2a), 2026-11-02:
- The bot is renamed to OSB and starts at version 2.0.0. The userscript header, the generated files (osb.user.js, osb.meta.js),
  the console tag, the download names and the panel title use the new name.
- Update checks, patch notes and navigation data come from github.com/corevider/osb instead of the upstream repository. The update check sends no user data,
  stays on by default, and can be switched off in Settings, Privacy ("Check GitHub for OSB updates"); when off it makes no request.
- Bug reports go to nobody by default: they are previewed, then copied or saved as a file. Since the opt-in release, a report is sent to api.osb.lol (Corevider) only when the
  player presses Send and confirms, and usage statistics are sent only after the player turns them on in Settings. The upstream report endpoint, the
  Discord link and the upstream site links are removed. Nothing is sent to nixxane or any third party.
- Share codes and files made by the nixxane bot still import. New exports use the app name osb.
- The OSB seal in the panel title bar and as the script icon, and the OSB README, docs and brand files.
- Maintenance files for OSB: AGENTS.md, docs/MAINTAINING.md, UPSTREAM.json and the workflows under .github/.
- The browser test harness is brought up to date with the current panel.
- With bag selling on, town trips sell the character bag before pet loot (also proposed upstream as nixxane/opensro-bot-lean#94).
- Choosing a town on the Town page sets up the town trip at once, and switching the town trip on fills what is missing; the "Set up this town" button is removed.
- Wear better gear (OSB-only fixes, 2026-11-03): it runs before the weapon merchant sells, each piece competes only for its own worn slot, and a piece the game refuses to wear is kept unsold. The "Pick up drops" checkbox is the first control on the Loot page.
- Gear level requirement (OSB-only fix, 2026-11-04): a requirement given as a mastery level (types 257-259, 273-276, 513-518) is read as that level, so wear better gear and the level deposit rule see such gear.
- The upstream port of 1.2.222 to 1.2.224 leaves out the report rate-limit change in lean-reports.js, because it belonged to the upstream report endpoint, which OSB does not use. The OSB server applies its own limits.
- The upstream port of 1.2.225 to 1.2.227 adapts two changes: loot moved from a nearly full pet to the bag is remembered and stored
  or sold on the next town trip like pet loot, and the share format is 2 so that older share codes keep the reverse scroll numbers
  they were made with. An old merchant reverse switch also carries its numbers to the Item mall switch.
- The upstream port of 1.2.228 to 1.2.231 takes the window layout fixes of 1.2.230 but not its browser test edits, which
  target upstream's own labels. Zero-setup leveling keeps its per-character record out of share codes.

Each port of upstream changes updates the base commit, the version and the date above, and UPSTREAM.json.
